            {
              "id": "4653a910-7702-305e-b8ab-fc8517c8196a",
              "name": "Potential SSRF Vulnerability: User Input Affects HttpClient Request",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Potential SSRF Vulnerability: User Input Affects HttpClient Request\" vulnerability in C# programming language refers to a situation where an attacker can manipulate the `HttpClient` request by injecting malicious data into the user input. This can lead to Server Side Request Forgery (SSRF) attacks, where the attacker can make requests to internal resources, bypassing firewalls and accessing sensitive data.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to validate, filter, or sanitize user input before using it in the `HttpClient` request. Avoid using user input directly in the request. If it's necessary to use user input, ensure it's properly validated and sanitized to prevent malicious data injection.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a simple fix for the vulnerability:\n\n```csharp\n// Assume user input is stored in variable userInput\nstring userInput = ...;\n\n// Validate and sanitize user input\nif (!Uri.TryCreate(userInput, UriKind.Absolute, out Uri validatedUri))\n{\n    throw new InvalidOperationException(\"Invalid URL\");\n}\n\n// Use validatedUri in HttpClient request\nusing var response = await _httpClient.PostAsync(validatedUri, requestContent, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- `System.Net.Http` for `HttpClient`\n- `System` for `Uri`\n\n## OWASP and CWE Resources\n\n- [OWASP Server Side Request Forgery Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Server_Side_Request_Forgery_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-918: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/918.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-918",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/918.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-918"
                ]
              }
            },
